---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/asbj31.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Identifying Estimates With a Risk of Material Adjustment" },
        { id: "s4", label: "What Must Be Disclosed for Each Identified Estimate" },
        { id: "s5", label: "A Principles-Based, Not Overly Prescriptive, Requirement" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Distinguishing This From Auditor-Reported Key Audit Matters" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Identifying a Significant Estimate" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — the Resulting Disclosure" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
      
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Helping readers understand where next year's numbers could meaningfully change</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 31 requires companies to DISCLOSE information about SIGNIFICANT accounting ESTIMATES made in the CURRENT year's financial statements that carry a genuine RISK of MATERIAL ADJUSTMENT in the FOLLOWING year — helping readers understand WHERE the financial statements are MOST sensitive to changes in JUDGEMENT or underlying assumptions, BEFORE such changes actually occur.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">All companies with significant estimation uncertainty in their financial statements</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies whose financial statements INCLUDE accounting ESTIMATES carrying a genuine risk of MATERIAL adjustment WITHIN the next fiscal year — a genuinely BROAD scope, given how COMMONLY estimation is embedded throughout financial reporting.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>Identifying Estimates With a Risk of Material Adjustment</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A forward-looking risk assessment, not a backward-looking summary</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Companies must IDENTIFY which SPECIFIC accounting estimates — for example, impairment assessments, actuarial assumptions, revenue variable consideration estimates, or deferred tax asset recoverability judgements — carry a genuine, FORWARD-LOOKING risk that a MATERIAL adjustment could be required in the NEXT fiscal year, based on how SENSITIVE the estimate is to changes in underlying ASSUMPTIONS or new INFORMATION.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>What Must Be Disclosed for Each Identified Estimate</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">The nature, assumptions, and risk factors — not necessarily a full sensitivity analysis</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">For EACH identified SIGNIFICANT estimate, companies disclose: the NATURE of the estimate and WHY it carries estimation uncertainty; the METHOD and KEY assumptions used; and INFORMATION helping users understand the extent to which the estimate could CHANGE materially in the FOLLOWING year — WITHOUT necessarily requiring a FULL, quantitative sensitivity analysis in every case, reflecting the PRINCIPLES-BASED nature of this requirement (Section 5).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>A Principles-Based, Not Overly Prescriptive, Requirement</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Judgement-driven disclosure, tailored to each company's own circumstances</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">This Statement is DELIBERATELY principles-based — it does NOT PRESCRIBE a rigid, one-size-fits-all disclosure FORMAT or REQUIRE quantitative sensitivity ranges in every case. Instead, companies EXERCISE judgement in determining WHICH estimates warrant disclosure and WHAT specific information best conveys the NATURE and EXTENT of the risk to READERS, given their OWN particular circumstances.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Distinguishing This From Auditor-Reported Key Audit Matters</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A management disclosure, not an auditor reporting requirement</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">This Statement's disclosure requirement is a MANAGEMENT disclosure OBLIGATION, appearing WITHIN the financial statement notes THEMSELVES — GENUINELY DISTINCT from "KEY AUDIT MATTERS" (KAM), which is a SEPARATE AUDITOR reporting requirement appearing in the AUDIT REPORT, reflecting the AUDITOR's OWN professional judgement about WHAT mattered MOST in the audit. Though the TWO concepts often OVERLAP in PRACTICE (an area of significant estimation uncertainty disclosed by MANAGEMENT under this Statement is often ALSO identified as a key audit matter by the AUDITOR), they serve GENUINELY different reporting PURPOSES and come from DIFFERENT reporting PARTIES.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — Identifying a Significant Estimate</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Recognising an estimate with genuine forward-looking risk</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A goodwill impairment assessment</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company carries ¥3,000,000,000 of goodwill relating to a business unit whose recent performance has been below plan, making the recoverable amount assessment highly sensitive to revised future cash flow projections.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The company IDENTIFIES this goodwill impairment ASSESSMENT as a SIGNIFICANT estimate carrying a genuine risk of MATERIAL adjustment in the NEXT fiscal year, warranting DISCLOSURE under this Statement.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — the Resulting Disclosure</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Conveying the nature and risk, without necessarily a full sensitivity table</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: The disclosure note for the goodwill assessment</div>
          <div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The company discloses: the ¥3,000,000,000 goodwill balance and the CASH-GENERATING UNIT it relates to; the KEY assumptions underlying the recoverable amount calculation (growth rates, discount rate); and a QUALITATIVE statement that a REASONABLY POSSIBLE change in these assumptions COULD result in a MATERIAL impairment being recognised in the NEXT fiscal year — giving readers a CLEAR sense of the RISK WITHOUT necessarily providing a full numeric sensitivity table.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 31 requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Identification of significant accounting estimates carrying a risk of material adjustment</span>
          <span>Nature of the estimate, key assumptions, and information conveying the extent of the risk</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Which estimates genuinely carry a risk of material adjustment, warranting separate disclosure</span>
              <span>What level of detail (qualitative vs quantitative) best conveys the risk to readers</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>This Statement is itself a disclosure requirement ABOUT estimates, rather than a measurement standard generating its own estimates</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IAS 1</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Feature</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 31)</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IAS 1, paragraphs 125–133)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Disclosure objective</span>
            <span>Sources of estimation uncertainty carrying material adjustment risk</span>
            <span>Same objective — converged</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Level of prescription</span>
            <span>Principles-based, judgement-driven</span>
            <span>Principles-based, judgement-driven — converged</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This is another genuinely CONVERGED, current-standard-aligned area — reflecting the SAME broader international trend toward enhanced TRANSPARENCY around key judgemental areas of financial reporting.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every significant estimate disclosure lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Significant estimate disclosure</span>
            <span>Notes only</span>
            <span>No effect on the primary financial statement figures themselves</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13">
      <span class="num">13</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 24</span>
            <span>Accounting Changes and Error Corrections — a related disclosure area addressing changes once they occur, complementing this Statement's forward-looking risk disclosure</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14">
      <span class="num">14</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Significant accounting estimate</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">An estimate in the current year's financial statements carrying a genuine risk of material adjustment in the following fiscal year.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">Key Audit Matter (KAM)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A separate auditor reporting concept identifying matters of most significance in the audit, distinct from this Statement's management disclosure requirement, though often overlapping in practice.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
